.policy "celery-practice-unknown-task-name" revision 1
.description "Name Celery tasks by strings that match a registered task; a worker discards messages for unknown names, so a mistyped beat entry never runs."
.language python
.mode log
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Rerail's own rule, not a port. Celery sends only a task's name; the worker looks it up in its registry, and for a
// name no task registered it logs "Received unregistered task of type ..." and discards the message
// (celery/worker/consumer/consumer.py, UNKNOWN_TASK_ERROR). A beat entry whose "task" has a typo, or names a task that
// was renamed or moved to another module, is sent on schedule and dropped every time: the job silently never runs.
// Reported, at the naming site, when no task of the run is registered under the name and the run owns it:
//   - the first argument (or `name=`) of `send_task(...)` on a Celery app (lib/celery's cel_app_ref or cel_app_value:
//     a resolved app, a factory's result, current_app, `self.app`), of celery's `signature(...)` and of
//     `<app>.signature(...)`;
//   - the "task" of a beat schedule entry: a dict (a literal or `dict(...)`) with a "task" and a "schedule" key
//     (Celery's documented entry shape), or with a "task" and an "options" key when its value reaches the beat
//     setting: it lies in a beat_schedule setting's value (lib/celery's cel_setting), in an item assigned to or an
//     `.update(...)` of that setting, in a module constant one of those reads (through imports, `**` splats
//     included), or in a run function such a value calls, or one it reaches through the call graph (paperless-ngx
//     lists its entries with "options" in `parse_beat_schedule()` and adds each cron from the environment).
// The name is a string literal, or a constant the engine resolves: a module constant of the run (through imports,
// re-exports and module aliases), a class attribute (`ExportTask.name`) or a local of its function, each bound once.
// A task is registered under its `name=` (such a value), else under <module>.<def>, which a string matches also by a
// dotted tail; `app.task(fn)` and `shared_task(name=...)(fn)` called as functions register the same way. A class
// deriving from celery's Task (through the run's classes, or `<app>.Task`) is registered under its `name = ...`
// attribute (such a value), else <module>.<Class>; a class whose `name` does not resolve registers nothing. The run
// owns a name n when n's module part (before the last dot) is exactly a module of the run, or when the run registers
// tasks under explicit dotted names that share n's first segment (`name="reports.scheduler"`). When a task with n's
// last segment as its def name exists elsewhere (a moved task), the message names it.
//   "task": "proj.tasks.shipp"          reported (proj/tasks.py defines `ship`)
//   app.send_task("proj.tasks.ship")    not reported (`@shared_task def ship` in proj/tasks.py)
//   app.send_task("billing.charge")     not reported (no module `billing` in the run: another service's task)
//   remote.send_task("tasks.upload")    not reported (the run has `proj/tasks.py`, but no module `tasks`)
//   ML_JOBS = [{"task": "proj.x.y", "options": {...}}]   not reported (never reaches the beat setting)
// Left alone: Celery's own tasks (`celery.*`, the names celery/app/builtins.py registers; the one name list kept,
// since a run module named `celery` would otherwise own them); a library's tasks (`django_celery_beat.*`), unowned
// unless the library is part of the run, where its tasks are registered; names whose module part is not a module of
// the run and whose first segment no explicit task name shares (another service's tasks: send_task is often used
// exactly for that); `send_task` on an object that is no Celery app; names built at runtime (f-strings, parameters,
// constants bound more than once); commented-out entries; test code (cel_test_doc).
// Gaps: tasks registered by a decorator wrapper that computes the name; a task name held by a constant outside the run;
// task modules autodiscovered from outside the run (an installed package); a run whose module names carry an extra
// leading package the worker does not (`api.tasks.x`, which the worker imports as `tasks.x`) does not own `tasks.*`;
// beat entries an app builds at runtime (`add_periodic_task`, django_celery_beat's PeriodicTask rows); whether the
// worker actually imports the module that defines the task (`include`/`imports`/autodiscover) is not checked.

#include "lib/celery.rerail"

.violation UnknownTaskName(at: node, n: symbol) "No task in this code registers \"{n}\", so a worker would discard it. Check it against the worker's registered tasks; leave it if another service or an installed package registers it."
.violation MovedTaskName(at: node, n: symbol, q: symbol) "No task registers \"{n}\"; a task \"{q}\" has its function name, so it may have moved. Check the worker's registered tasks; leave it if another service or a package registers it."
// What the run registers, owns and uses are facts of the whole run, over names alone (uk_unknown, uk_moved:
// cross_file). Each naming site is stated in its own file, with the string it holds (uk_ref) or the constant it reads
// (uk_ref_sym, a symbol another file binds: uk_const), and what it needs of other files (uk_holds).
UnknownTaskName(at, n) :- uk_ref(at, n, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk), uk_unknown(n), !uk_moved(n, _), uk_live(at).
UnknownTaskName(at, n) :- uk_ref_sym(at, q, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk), uk_const(q, n), uk_unknown(n), !uk_moved(n, _),
    uk_live(at).
MovedTaskName(at, n, q) :- uk_ref(at, n, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk), uk_unknown(n), uk_moved(n, q), uk_live(at).
MovedTaskName(at, n, mq) :- uk_ref_sym(at, q, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk), uk_const(q, n), uk_unknown(n),
    uk_moved(n, mq), uk_live(at).
.decl uk_live(at: node)
uk_live(at) :- docof(at, d), !cel_test_doc(d).

// ---- needs -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_holds(q, k): lib/celery's cel_is, and this rule's own kinds, closed over the run by symbol: "uk_beat_var" (a
// module variable whose value reaches the beat setting), "uk_beat_fn" (a run function whose result reaches it) and
// "uk_tcls" (celery's Task, or a class of the run deriving from it or from `<app>.Task`). It spans files on purpose
// (a beat setting reads a constant another module binds); symbols alone: cross_file.
.decl uk_holds(q: symbol, k: symbol) cross_file
uk_holds(q, k) :- cel_is(q, k).
uk_holds(q, "uk_beat_var") :- uk_var_beat_if(q, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk).
uk_holds(q, "uk_beat_var") :- uk_var_read(q, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk).
uk_holds(gq, "uk_beat_fn") :- uk_fn_call(gq, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk).
uk_holds(hq, "uk_beat_fn") :- uk_holds(gq, "uk_beat_fn"), reach(gq, hq).
uk_holds("celery.Task", "uk_tcls"). uk_holds("celery.app.task.Task", "uk_tcls").
uk_holds(q, "uk_tcls") :- uk_tcls_if(q, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk).

// ---- values ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_str_here(v, n): v is the string n, or a local name of its own function bound once to it. uk_str_sym(v, q): v is
// a name or attribute resolving to q, a module constant of the run (cel_sym follows imports, re-exports and module
// aliases) or a class attribute (`Cls.name`), whose value uk_const states in its own file.
.decl uk_str_here(v: node, n: symbol)
uk_str_here(v, n) :- str(v, n).
uk_str_here(v, n) :- unparen(v, u), kind(u, "identifier"), text(u, x), look(u, x, s), !kind(s, "module"),
    asg(s, x, w, _), str(w, n), count : { asg(s, x, _, _) } = 1.
.decl uk_str_sym(v: node, q: symbol)
uk_str_sym(v, q) :- unparen(v, u), (kind(u, "identifier") ; kind(u, "attribute")), cel_sym(u, q).
// uk_const(q, n): q, a module constant or a class attribute bound once, is the string n. Stated in q's own file.
.decl uk_const(q: symbol, n: symbol)
uk_const(@dot(mq, x), n) :- modnode(_, m), modname(m, mq), asg(m, x, w, _), str(w, n), count : { asg(m, x, _, _) } = 1.
uk_const(@dot(cq, x), n) :- class_def(c, cq), asg(c, x, w, _), str(w, n), count : { asg(c, x, _, _) } = 1.

// ---- the names the run uses --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_site(e, how, nq, nk): expression e is where a task is named: send_task's first argument or `name=`,
// signature's first argument, a beat entry's "task".
.decl uk_site(e: node, how: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_site(e, "send_task", nq, nk) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, "send_task"),
    unparen(o, u), (cel_app_ref(u, nq, nk) ; cel_app_value(u, nq, nk)), (posarg(c, 0, e) ; call_arg(c, -1, "name", e)).
uk_site(e, "signature", "", "") :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), sym_of(fn, q),
    (q = "celery.signature" ; q = "celery.canvas.signature" ; q = "celery.canvas.Signature" ; q = "celery.Signature" ;
    q = "celery.subtask" ; q = "celery.canvas.subtask"),
    posarg(c, 0, e).
uk_site(e, "signature", nq, nk) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), attr_of(fn, o, "signature"),
    unparen(o, u), (cel_app_ref(u, nq, nk) ; cel_app_value(u, nq, nk)), posarg(c, 0, e).
uk_site(e, "beat", "", "") :- uk_entry_key(m, "task", e), uk_entry_key(m, "schedule", _).
uk_site(e, "beat", nq, nk) :- uk_entry_key(m, "task", e), uk_entry_key(m, "options", _), uk_beat_part(m, nq, nk).
// uk_entry_key(m, k, v): m is a dict literal with the string key k, or a `dict(...)` call with the keyword k; v its
// value.
.decl uk_entry_key(m: node, k: symbol, v: node)
uk_entry_key(m, k, v) :- kind(m, "dictionary"), child(m, p, _), kind(p, "pair"), field(p, "key", kn), str(kn, k),
    field(p, "value", v).
uk_entry_key(m, k, v) :- kind(m, "call"), field(m, "function", f), builtin_ref(f, "dict"), call_arg(m, -1, k, v).
// ---- what reaches the beat setting -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_beat_expr(e, nq, nk): e's value reaches the beat setting: a beat_schedule setting's value, the value of an item
// assigned to the setting or of its `.update(...)`, the value of a module constant that reaches it ("uk_beat_var":
// one read in a beat expression or in a beat function, through imports).
.decl uk_beat_expr(e: node, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_beat_expr(u, "", "") :- cel_setting("beat_schedule", v, _), unparen(v, u).
uk_beat_expr(u, nq, nk) :- kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), kind(l, "subscript"), field(l, "value", t),
    uk_beat_target(t, nq, nk), field(a, "right", v), unparen(v, u).
uk_beat_expr(u, nq, nk) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), attr_of(f, t, "update"),
    uk_beat_target(t, nq, nk), call_arg(c, _, _, v), unparen(v, u).
uk_beat_expr(u, q, "uk_beat_var") :- cel_module_var(q, w), unparen(w, u).
// uk_beat_read(r, nq, nk): r is a beat expression or lies in one.
.decl uk_beat_read(r: node, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_beat_read(e, nq, nk) :- uk_beat_expr(e, nq, nk).
uk_beat_read(r, nq, nk) :- uk_beat_expr(e, nq, nk), within(r, e).
// uk_var_beat_if(q, nq, nk): module variable q's own value reaches the beat setting (a beat_schedule setting's
// value). uk_var_read(q, nq, nk): q is read in a beat expression, or in a function ("uk_beat_fn"). Each stated in
// its own file, by symbol.
.decl uk_var_beat_if(q: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_var_beat_if(q, nq, nk) :- cel_module_var(q, w), unparen(w, u), uk_beat_expr(u, nq, nk).
.decl uk_var_read(q: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_var_read(q, nq, nk) :- uk_beat_read(r, nq, nk), (kind(r, "identifier") ; kind(r, "attribute")), cel_run_var(r, q).
uk_var_read(q, gq, "uk_beat_fn") :- kind(g, "function_definition"), within(r, g),
    (kind(r, "identifier") ; kind(r, "attribute")), cel_run_var(r, q), qualname(g, gq).
// uk_fn_call(g, nq, nk): a beat expression calls run function g (`CELERY_BEAT_SCHEDULE = parse_beat_schedule()`); the
// functions g reaches through the call graph (python/calls' reach) are beat functions too (uk_holds).
.decl uk_fn_call(g: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_fn_call(gq, nq, nk) :- uk_beat_read(c, nq, nk), kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", f), cel_run_def(f, gq).
// uk_beat_target(t, nq, nk): t is the beat setting: `<x>.conf.beat_schedule`, or a name bound to a beat expression
// (`CELERY_BEAT_SCHEDULE`, a celeryconfig's `beat_schedule`).
.decl uk_beat_target(t: node, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_beat_target(t, "", "") :- attr_of(t, o, "beat_schedule"), attr_of(o, _, "conf").
uk_beat_target(t, q, "uk_beat_var") :- (kind(t, "identifier") ; kind(t, "attribute")), cel_run_var(t, q).
// uk_beat_part(m, nq, nk): dict m reaches the beat setting: it lies in a beat expression, or in a beat function.
.decl uk_beat_part(m: node, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_beat_part(m, nq, nk) :- uk_entry_key(m, "options", _), uk_beat_read(m, nq, nk).
uk_beat_part(m, gq, "uk_beat_fn") :- uk_entry_key(m, "options", _), kind(g, "function_definition"), within(m, g),
    qualname(g, gq).
// uk_ref(e, n, nq, nk): site e names the task n. uk_ref_sym(e, q, nq, nk): site e names the task uk_const(q, _).
.decl uk_ref(e: node, n: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_ref(e, n, nq, nk) :- uk_site(e, _, nq, nk), uk_str_here(e, n).
.decl uk_ref_sym(e: node, q: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_ref_sym(e, q, nq, nk) :- uk_site(e, _, nq, nk), uk_str_sym(e, q).

// ---- the names the run registers ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_reg(n, how): a task of the run is registered as n, "explicit" (a name= or a class's name attribute) or "implicit"
// (<module>.<def>, <module>.<Class>). A fact of the whole run (cross_file, names alone), from what each file states
// of its own tasks: uk_reg_here (a string), uk_reg_sym (a constant, uk_const).
.decl uk_reg(n: symbol, how: symbol) cross_file
uk_reg(n, how) :- uk_reg_here(n, how, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk).
uk_reg(n, how) :- uk_reg_sym(q, how, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk), uk_const(q, n).
.decl uk_reg_here(n: symbol, how: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
.decl uk_reg_sym(q: symbol, how: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_reg_here(n, "explicit", nq, nk) :- cel_task_option(_, "name", v, nq, nk), uk_str_here(v, n).
uk_reg_sym(q, "explicit", nq, nk) :- cel_task_option(_, "name", v, nq, nk), uk_str_sym(v, q).
uk_reg_here(n, "implicit", nq, nk) :- cel_task_name(f, n, nq, nk), !cel_task_named_opt(f).
// `app.task(fn)`, `app.task(fn, name=...)`, `shared_task(name=...)(fn)` called as functions, fn a def or class of
// the run.
uk_reg_here(n, "explicit", nq, nk) :- uk_wrap_call(c, nq, nk), uk_wrap_name(c, v), uk_str_here(v, n).
uk_reg_sym(q, "explicit", nq, nk) :- uk_wrap_call(c, nq, nk), uk_wrap_name(c, v), uk_str_sym(v, q).
uk_reg_here(q, "implicit", nq, nk) :- uk_wrap_call(c, nq, nk), !uk_wrap_named(c), posarg(c, 0, a), cel_run_def(a, q).
.decl uk_wrap_call(c: node, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_wrap_call(c, nq, nk) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", fn), cel_task_fn(fn, nq, nk), posarg(c, 0, a),
    cel_run_def(a, _).
uk_wrap_call(c, nq, nk) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", k), kind(k, "call"), field(k, "function", fn),
    cel_task_fn(fn, nq, nk), posarg(c, 0, a), cel_run_def(a, _).
.decl uk_wrap_name(c: node, v: node)
uk_wrap_name(c, v) :- kind(c, "call"), call_arg(c, -1, "name", v).
uk_wrap_name(c, v) :- kind(c, "call"), field(c, "function", k), kind(k, "call"), call_arg(k, -1, "name", v).
.decl uk_wrap_named(c: node)
uk_wrap_named(c) :- uk_wrap_name(c, _).
// A task class: registered under its `name` attribute (such a value), else <module>.<Class>.
uk_reg_here(n, "explicit", nq, nk) :- uk_task_class(c, nq, nk), uk_class_name_attr(c, v), uk_str_here(v, n).
uk_reg_sym(q, "explicit", nq, nk) :- uk_task_class(c, nq, nk), uk_class_name_attr(c, v), uk_str_sym(v, q).
uk_reg_here(@dot(mq, x), "implicit", nq, nk) :- uk_task_class(c, nq, nk), !uk_class_named(c), def_name(c, x),
    docof(c, d), doc(d, _, mq), mq != "", nearest(c, m, scope), kind(m, "module").
// uk_task_class(c, nq, nk): c derives from celery's Task, directly, through `<app>.Task`, or through the run's
// classes ("uk_tcls" of a base). uk_tcls_if: the same by symbol, for the classes deriving from c.
.decl uk_task_class(c: node, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_task_class(c, b, "uk_tcls") :- kind(c, "class_definition"), cel_class_base(c, b).
uk_task_class(c, nq, nk) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "superclasses", al), child(al, e, _),
    attr_of(e, o, "Task"), unparen(o, u), (cel_app_ref(u, nq, nk) ; cel_app_value(u, nq, nk)).
.decl uk_tcls_if(q: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_tcls_if(q, nq, nk) :- uk_task_class(c, nq, nk), class_def(c, q).
// uk_class_name_attr(c, v): `name = v` in c's body (any value: one that does not resolve registers no implicit name).
.decl uk_class_name_attr(c: node, v: node)
uk_class_name_attr(c, v) :- kind(c, "class_definition"), field(c, "body", b), body_stmt(b, s, _),
    kind(s, "expression_statement"), child(s, a, 0), kind(a, "assignment"), field(a, "left", l), text(l, "name"),
    field(a, "right", v).
.decl uk_class_named(c: node)
uk_class_named(c) :- uk_class_name_attr(c, _).

// ---- the names asked about ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_name(n): a string some site names a task by (a superset: whatever its site needs). uk_unknown(n): no task of
// the run registers n, the run owns n, and n is none of Celery's own. Facts of the whole run, over names alone.
.decl uk_name(n: symbol) cross_file
uk_name(n) :- uk_ref_name(n).
uk_name(n) :- uk_ref_const(q), uk_const(q, n).
.decl uk_ref_name(n: symbol)
uk_ref_name(n) :- uk_ref(_, n, _, _).
.decl uk_ref_const(q: symbol)
uk_ref_const(q) :- uk_ref_sym(_, q, _, _).
.decl uk_unknown(n: symbol) cross_file
uk_unknown(n) :- uk_name(n), !uk_known(n), uk_owned(n), !uk_celery_own(n).
.decl uk_known(n: symbol)
uk_known(n) :- uk_name(n), uk_reg(n, _).
uk_known(n) :- uk_name(n), uk_reg(q, "implicit"), suffix(cat(".", n), q).

// ---- ownership ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// uk_owned(n): n's module part is exactly a module of the run, or n's first segment is shared by an explicit dotted
// name. A module that merely ends with n's module part (`app.tasks` for `tasks.x`) does not own it: another service's
// worker may well have a top-level `tasks` module.
.decl uk_owned(n: symbol) cross_file
uk_owned(n) :- uk_name(n), split_dot(n, m, _), m != "", uk_module(m).
uk_owned(n) :- uk_name(n), split_dot(n, m, _), m != "", h = @head(n), uk_reg(x, "explicit"), x != h, @head(x) = h.
.decl uk_module(m: symbol)
uk_module(m) :- doc(_, _, m).
// uk_celery_own(n): Celery's own tasks (celery/app/builtins.py registers them as `celery.*`).
.decl uk_celery_own(n: symbol)
uk_celery_own(n) :- uk_name(n), @head(n) = "celery".
// uk_moved(n, q): a task whose def is named for n's last segment is registered as q. Each file states its tasks' def
// names and registered names (uk_task_def).
.decl uk_moved(n: symbol, q: symbol) cross_file
uk_moved(n, q) :- uk_name(n), split_dot(n, _, x), uk_task_def(x, q, nq, nk), uk_holds(nq, nk), q != n.
.decl uk_task_def(x: symbol, q: symbol, nq: symbol, nk: symbol)
uk_task_def(x, q, nq, nk) :- cel_task(f, nq, nk), def_name(f, x), cel_task_name(f, q, nq, nk).

// The cases, `upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/`: one repository in which each line
// ending in `# caught` is reported and no other line.
.test cases exactly
    .fixture "proj/__init__.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/__init__.py"
    .fixture "proj/celery.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/celery.py"
    .fixture "proj/classes.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/classes.py"
    .fixture "proj/client.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/client.py"
    .fixture "proj/contract.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/contract.py"
    .fixture "proj/factory.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/factory.py"
    .fixture "proj/jobs.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/jobs.py"
    .fixture "proj/maintenance.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/maintenance.py"
    .fixture "proj/metrics.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/metrics.py"
    .fixture "proj/schedule.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/schedule.py"
    .fixture "proj/settings.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/settings.py"
    .fixture "proj/tasks.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/tasks.py"
    .fixture "proj/tests/__init__.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/tests/__init__.py"
    .fixture "proj/tests/test_beat.py" from "../upstream/celery-practice/authored/celery-practice-unknown-task-name/proj/tests/test_beat.py"
